Now lap logic. Current:

```js
    car.distance += car.speed * dt;
    car.progress = modulo(car.distance, TRACK);
    car.topSpeed = Math.max(car.topSpeed, car.speed);

    if (car.distance >= TRACK * car.lap) {
      const lapTime = raceTime - car.lapStart;
      car.lapStart = raceTime;
      car.lapTimes.push(lapTime);
      if (!car.best || lapTime < car.best) car.best = lapTime;
      const completed = car.lap;
      car.lap = Math.min(LAPS, car.lap + 1);
      if (completed >= LAPS) {
        finishRace();
        return;
      }
      if (car.lap === LAPS) showMessage('FINAL LAP', 1700);
      else showMessage(`LAP ${pad(car.lap)}  ·  ${fmtTime(lapTime)}`, 2000);
      if (soundOn) beep(760, .08, 'sine', .03);
    }
```

New:

```js
    car.distance += car.speed * dt;
    car.progress = modulo(car.distance - GRID, TRACK);
    car.topSpeed = Math.max(car.topSpeed, car.speed);

    if (car.distance >= car.nextLine) {
      if (!car.raceStarted) {
        car.raceStarted = true;
        car.lapStart = raceTime;
        car.nextLine += TRACK;
        showMessage('LAP 01', 1200);
      } else {
        const lapTime = raceTime - car.lapStart;
        car.lapStart = raceTime;
        car.lapTimes.push(lapTime);
        if (!car.best || lapTime < car.best) car.best = lapTime;
        const completed = car.lap;
        car.nextLine += TRACK;
        car.lap = Math.min(LAPS, car.lap + 1);
        if (completed >= LAPS) { finishRace(); return; }
        if (car.lap === LAPS) showMessage('FINAL LAP', 1700);
        else showMessage(`LAP ${pad(car.lap)}  ·  ${fmtTime(lapTime)}`, 2000);
        if (soundOn) beep(760, .08, 'sine', .03);
      }
    }
```

Wait at the finish: when completed = LAPS (3) and distance >= GRID + 3TRACK, lap stays 3; finish. Good. But `car.lap` increments to 4 then min 3. Fine.

The first crossing at GRID occurs after 88m (~1s). It sets raceStarted and lapStart. The lap count remains 1. Good. The first lap then ends at GRID+TRACK.

Potential multiple crossings in one frame? speed ~80, dt .05 → 4m, no.

Now AI finish threshold RACE_END.

Physics push multiplier 1.05 → .62.

Progress debug skip.

Also `updateRev` uses car.progress no.

`liveRank` fine.

HUD timer keeps raceTime. At finish, raceTime includes grid offset.

Rivals at start have progress absolute from grid; fine.

Rival finish: `o.progress >= RACE_END`.

Update drawStartArea: `ahead` at start=88; the line appears 88m ahead. Good.

Corner label at start progress=5705 → p=.9847 → we set >.975 → START/FINISH. Good.

One more: in resetRace, updateHUD shows lap 01, pos 08, corner start. Good.

Patch.

