Start grid: rivals' lateral ±.28 in two columns, but since the player starts at lateral 0 (center) and the line is ahead, the player is in the middle behind two columns—not a real grid slot. In F1, the grid alternates left/right; P8 would be on one side. Set player start lateral = -0.28? But the player should have freedom to choose; starting centered is fine though. Actually with rivals in two columns at ±.28, the player centered looks like P8 in the middle of a 3-wide grid. Better set player initial lateral = -0.28 and adjust rivals' lateral by index alternating ±0.28. Then the player lines up behind the left column, realistic. But the car can move freely. Set car.lateral=-.28 at setup. However, the start camera and controls; fine. The car at -0.28*0.37W = -0.104W left of center. Good.

Rivals: gap 16..72; lateral alternating. Two columns. Player P8 at -.28, but the car immediately ahead at gap 16 is also lateral .28? Set rivals i=6 (gap16) lateral -0.28? In a staggered grid, P7 and P8 are on opposite sides. Opponents array i=0 leader gap72 lateral .28, i=1 .28? Currently i%2 ? .28 : -.28 → i0 -.28, i1 .28,... i6 -.28. Player at -.28 would be directly behind i6. Real grids: consecutive cars alternate sides. P7 (gap16) is i6 at -.28, so P8 should be .28. Set car.lateral=.28. Then the player starts right side. Good.

